    /// <summary>Tweak a secret key by adding tweak to it.</summary>
    /// <param name="ctx">pointer to a context object. In/Out: seckey: pointer to a 32-byte secret key. If the secret key is invalid according to secp256k1_ec_seckey_verify, this function returns 0. seckey will be set to some unspecified value if this function returns 0. In:    tweak32: pointer to a 32-byte tweak, which must be valid according to secp256k1_ec_seckey_verify or 32 zero bytes. For uniformly random 32-byte tweaks, the chance of being invalid is negligible (around 1 in 2^128).</param>
